{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze felt like my strongest next choice because its Clapton connection and relaxed blues sound connect directly with my interest in Old Sock.",
    "Step Back fits the guitar-focused blues side of my recent Clapton and Hendrix listening. Revelator also appeals if it is the Tedeschi Trucks Band album, though I would only choose The Breeze today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Jackie Gleason's orchestral music and Live At The Bon Soir's vocal nightclub performance do not offer the guitar-led rock and blues I want right now.",
    "The early country collection feels too far from my current listening, while Louis Jordan's jump blues shares a blues connection but does not satisfy my present interest in guitar-focused music.",
    "I cannot confidently connect III, Better Word, or Time to my interests from those titles alone, so I would pass rather than assume they fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to stretch my interest in established musicians into a broader appetite for older orchestral, vocal, and country recordings.",
    "A broad blues connection seems to count too much when the guitar sound and style are what make a recommendation appealing to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The direct connection to Clapton and Old Sock matters more to my choice today than a loose connection to older music.",
    "My recent listening points toward guitar-led blues and rock, with room for a relaxed or soulful sound.",
    "I rarely act on recommendations, so an item needs a clear connection to my listening; even several plausible matches would still lead me to choose just one today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You partly understood my interest in blues and rock, but extended it too broadly beyond the guitar sound and artist connections that matter to me today."
}"}
